# the row of a quotient of integers says between which two integers it lies. Folding puts the number itself in the place of the quotient.
# The type of a number with a fraction names the two integers around it: the least type that holds it. So it lies within whatever a row says of the operation that was folded,
# and so does what a built-in or an operator makes of it. The head of the loop holds what enters, 0, joined with what the walk saw come round, and every back edge is held against it
# function run(n) { let q = 0, t = 0, s = 0, m = 0; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { q = 7 / 3; t = Math.trunc(7 / 3); s = 7 / 3 + 1; m = -(7 / 3); } return [q, t, s, m]; }
